{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Weight decomposition of $\\langle HWS| e^{a_{13}E_{13}} e^{a_{14}E_{14}} e^{a_{23}E_{23}} e^{a_{24}E_{24}}$\n\nThe four generators $E_{13},E_{14},E_{23},E_{24}$ span the abelian nilpotent subalgebra $\\mathfrak{n}^+_{\\,\\{1,2\\}\\times\\{3,4\\}}$: since\n$[E_{ij},E_{kl}] = \\delta_{jk}E_{il}-\\delta_{li}E_{kj}$ and here $i,k\\in\\{1,2\\}$, $j,l\\in\\{3,4\\}$ are drawn from *disjoint* index sets, every Kronecker delta vanishes. Hence **all four commute**, the four exponentials merge into $\\exp[\\sum a_{ij}E_{ij}]$, and the monomial expansion is a plain multinomial with no ordering ambiguity:\n$$\\langle HWS|\\,e^{\\sum a_{ij}E_{ij}} \\;=\\; \\sum_{n_{13},n_{14},n_{23},n_{24}\\ge 0}\\ \\prod_{ij}\\frac{a_{ij}^{n_{ij}}}{n_{ij}!}\\ \\langle HWS|\\,E_{13}^{n_{13}}E_{14}^{n_{14}}E_{23}^{n_{23}}E_{24}^{n_{24}}.$$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Weight grading\n\nA covector $\\langle HWS|E_{13}$ pairs nontrivially only with kets of weight $\\lambda-e_1+e_3$ (because $E_{13}$ must raise that ket back to $|HWS\\rangle$). So the monomial labelled by $n=(n_{13},n_{14},n_{23},n_{24})$ sits in the weight space\n$$\\nu(n) \\;=\\; \\lambda \\;-\\;(n_{13}+n_{14})\\,e_1\\;-\\;(n_{23}+n_{24})\\,e_2\\;+\\;(n_{13}+n_{23})\\,e_3\\;+\\;(n_{14}+n_{24})\\,e_4 .$$\nSo the weight only sees the four margins\n$$m_1=n_{13}+n_{14},\\quad m_2=n_{23}+n_{24},\\quad m_3=n_{13}+n_{23},\\quad m_4=n_{14}+n_{24},\\qquad m_1+m_2=m_3+m_4 ,$$\ni.e. the row/column sums of the $2\\times2$ table $\\binom{n_{13}\\ n_{14}}{n_{23}\\ n_{24}}$. A weight sector is therefore *degenerate*: fixing $(m_1,m_2,m_3,m_4)$ leaves the one-parameter family $n_{13}=t$, $n_{14}=m_1-t$, $n_{23}=m_3-t$, $n_{24}=m_2-m_3+t$ with $\\max(0,m_3-m_2)\\le t\\le\\min(m_1,m_3)$ — exactly $\\min(m_1,m_2,m_3,m_4)+1$ monomials per weight.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* --- gl(4) generators in the Gelfand-Tsetlin basis (ported verbatim from Hamiltonians_SU4.wb) --- *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #] & /@ (Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]))}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse@Sort@res, Reverse@Sort@Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]], l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]], l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#]] & /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]], l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep], l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nEE[rep_][i_, j_] := JJ[i, j, rep];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Sanity: the four generators pairwise commute, and each annihilates |HWS> (they are raising ops). *)\ntestrep = {3, 2, 1, 0};\nidx = {{1, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}};\ncomms = Table[EE[testrep] @@ p . EE[testrep] @@ q - EE[testrep] @@ q . EE[testrep] @@ p, {p, idx}, {q, idx}];\nhws = UnitVector[dim[testrep], 1];  (* ps[{rep}] is reverse-sorted, so pattern 1 is the HWS *)\n{Max[Abs[Flatten[comms]]], Max[Abs[Flatten[Table[EE[testrep] @@ p . hws, {p, idx}]]]], J0[#][ps[{testrep}][[1]]] & /@ Range[4]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"550921\" data-output-id=\"8\" data-out-n=\"56\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"3\" data-sub-start=\"5\" data-sub-end=\"5\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[56]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered wl-lb-pending\" data-lb-id=\"lb-ms0hut7y-x329e4y\" data-page-width-em=\"80\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezAsMCxcbGVmdFx7MywyLDEsMFxyaWdodFx9XHJpZ2h0XH0=\" style=\"opacity:0.65;transition:opacity 0.35s\"><div class=\"wl-lb-content\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[56]= \\left\\{0,0,\\left\\{3,2,1,0\\right\\}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "28ed22b8-b0e3-4172-8ab2-2efb7fb259d7"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### The grading routines\n\n`nList[d]` enumerates exponent tuples $n=(n_{13},n_{14},n_{23},n_{24})$ of total degree $d$; `wt[\\lambda,n]` is $\\nu(n)$; `sectors[\\lambda,d]` groups the degree-$d$ monomials into weight sectors, each entry being the list of $\\{$coefficient, exponents$\\}$ that share a weight. `braExp[\\lambda,d]` is the truncated expansion written weight-sector by weight-sector.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Exponent tuples of total degree d, the weight they carry, and the multinomial coefficient. *)\nnList[d_] := Flatten[Table[{n13, n14, n23, d - n13 - n14 - n23}, {n13, 0, d}, {n14, 0, d - n13}, {n23, 0, d - n13 - n14}], 2];\nwt[lam_, {n13_, n14_, n23_, n24_}] := lam + {-(n13 + n14), -(n23 + n24), n13 + n23, n14 + n24};\ncoef[{n13_, n14_, n23_, n24_}] := a[1, 3]^n13 a[1, 4]^n14 a[2, 3]^n23 a[2, 4]^n24/(n13! n14! n23! n24!);\n\n(* Weight sectors at fixed total degree d: association weight -> list of exponent tuples. *)\nsectors[lam_, d_] := GroupBy[nList[d], wt[lam, #] &];\n\n(* Same sector labelled directly by the margins m={m1,m2,m3,m4} (needs m1+m2==m3+m4);\n   the free parameter t=n13 runs over min(m)+1 values. *)\nmarginSector[{m1_, m2_, m3_, m4_}] := If[m1 + m2 =!= m3 + m4, {},\n   Table[{t, m1 - t, m3 - t, m2 - m3 + t}, {t, Max[0, m3 - m2], Min[m1, m3]}]];\n\n(* Symbolic bra expansion truncated at total degree dmax, organised by weight sector:\n   each entry is weight -> sum over that sector of coef[n] * bra[n]. *)\nbraExp[lam_, dmax_] := Association @@ Flatten[Table[\n    Normal@Map[Total[coef[#] bra @@ # & /@ #] &, sectors[lam, d]] , {d, 0, dmax}]];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Numerical verification in an explicit irrep\n\nThree things to check in $\\lambda=\\{3,2,1,0\\}$ (dim 64): (i) the product of the four exponentials equals $\\exp[\\sum a_{ij}E_{ij}]$; (ii) each monomial $\\langle HWS|E_{13}^{n_{13}}\\cdots$ is supported *only* on GT patterns of weight $\\nu(n)$, confirming the grading formula; (iii) sector sizes match $\\min(m)+1$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (i) The four exponentials really do merge into one (nilpotent => MatrixExp is polynomial).\n   Checked at rational parameter values to keep the 64x64 exponentials cheap. *)\navals = {7/5, -3/2, 11/7, 2/9};\ngens = EE[testrep] @@@ {{1, 3}, {1, 4}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}};\nlhs = Dot @@ (MatrixExp[#1 #2] & @@@ Transpose[{avals, gens}]);\nrhs = MatrixExp[avals . gens];\nMax[Abs[lhs - rhs]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"550921\" data-output-id=\"11\" data-out-n=\"77\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"7\" data-sub-start=\"6\" data-sub-end=\"6\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[77]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered wl-lb-pending\" data-lb-id=\"lb-ms0hv1m1-qn32hs0\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"MA==\" style=\"opacity:0.65;transition:opacity 0.35s\"><div class=\"wl-lb-content\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[77]= 0",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "f1ffc368-1198-492d-87ab-acec7f52cc49"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (ii) Grading check: the GT patterns supporting each bra monomial all carry weight nu(n).\n   mpow avoids MatrixPower[nilpotent, 0], which throws MatrixPower::sing. *)\nmpow[m_, 0] := IdentityMatrix[Length[m]];\nmpow[m_, n_] := MatrixPower[m, n];\npatWt[pat_] := J0[#][pat] & /@ Range[4];\nallWts = patWt /@ ps[{testrep}];\nbraVec[rep_, {n13_, n14_, n23_, n24_}] := UnitVector[dim[rep], 1] . mpow[EE[rep][1, 3], n13] . mpow[EE[rep][1, 4], n14] . mpow[EE[rep][2, 3], n23] . mpow[EE[rep][2, 4], n24];\ngradeCheck[rep_, lam_, n_] := Module[{v = braVec[rep, n], supp},\n   supp = DeleteDuplicates[Pick[allWts, Unitize[v], 1]];\n   supp === {} || supp === {wt[lam, n]}];\n(* nonzero monomials, and whether every one of them is correctly graded *)\n{Count[Flatten[Table[braVec[testrep, n] =!= 0 Range[dim[testrep]], {d, 0, 6}, {n, nList[d]}], 1], True],\n And @@ Flatten[Table[gradeCheck[testrep, testrep, n], {d, 0, 6}, {n, nList[d]}]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"550921\" data-output-id=\"12\" data-out-n=\"84\" data-sub-idx=\"8\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"8\" data-sub-start=\"11\" data-sub-end=\"12\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[84]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered wl-lb-pending\" data-lb-id=\"lb-ms0hv5it-j7l0vc0\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRcezM0LFxtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX1ccmlnaHRcfQ==\" style=\"opacity:0.65;transition:opacity 0.35s\"><div class=\"wl-lb-content\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">34</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[84]= \\left\\{34,\\mathrm{True}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "8e280ff1-9d7d-4cd0-b830-3fa57c40b576"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (iii) Sector sizes: every weight sector has exactly min(m1,m2,m3,m4)+1 monomials,\n   and grouping by weight agrees with the margin parametrisation. *)\nmargins[{n13_, n14_, n23_, n24_}] := {n13 + n14, n23 + n24, n13 + n23, n14 + n24};\nTable[With[{s = sectors[{l1, l2, l3, l4}, d]},\n   And[\n    And @@ KeyValueMap[Length[#2] === Min[margins[First[#2]]] + 1 &, s],\n    And @@ (Sort[#] === Sort[marginSector[margins[First[#]]]] & /@ Values[s])]],\n  {d, 0, 8}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"550921\" data-output-id=\"14\" data-out-n=\"88\" data-sub-idx=\"2\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"9\" data-sub-start=\"3\" data-sub-end=\"7\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[88]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered wl-lb-pending\" data-lb-id=\"lb-ms0hv5u3-2rssfh5\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGxlZnRce1xtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX0sXG1hdGhybXtUcnVlfSxcbWF0aHJte1RydWV9LFxtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX0sXG1hdGhybXtUcnVlfSxcbWF0aHJte1RydWV9LFxtYXRocm17VHJ1ZX0sXG1hdGhybXtUcnVlfSxcbWF0aHJte1RydWV9XHJpZ2h0XH0=\" style=\"opacity:0.65;transition:opacity 0.35s\"><div class=\"wl-lb-content\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[88]= \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True},\\mathrm{True}\\right\\}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "27e96f83-74aa-443f-a36c-47e95f7b5e72"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Using it\n\n`sectorTable[\\lambda, d]` lists, for total degree $d$, each weight $\\nu$ together with its multiplicity and the collected symbolic coefficient. `sectorVec[rep, \\nu]` gives the actual covector in a concrete irrep, i.e. the weight-$\\nu$ component of $\\langle HWS|e^{\\sum a_{ij}E_{ij}}$ (a polynomial in the $a_{ij}$ times basis covectors) — which is the object to pair with kets when extracting CG coefficients.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Weight sectors at fixed total degree, with multiplicity and collected coefficient. *)\nsectorTable[lam_, d_] := TableForm[\n   KeyValueMap[{#1, Length[#2], Total[coef /@ #2]} &, KeySort@sectors[lam, d]],\n   TableHeadings -> {None, {\"weight nu\", \"mult\", \"sum of coef[n]\"}}];\n\nsectorTable[{l1, l2, l3, l4}, 4]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* The weight-nu component of <HWS| Exp[Sum a_ij E_ij] in a concrete irrep:\n   sum over the sector of coef[n] * (bra monomial). Truncation is automatic --\n   monomials outside the rep vanish. *)\nsectorVec[rep_, lam_, nu_] := Module[{m = {lam[[1]] - nu[[1]], lam[[2]] - nu[[2]], nu[[3]] - lam[[3]], nu[[4]] - lam[[4]]}},\n   Total[coef[#] braVec[rep, #] & /@ marginSector[m]]];\n\n(* Example: two-step-down weight sectors in lambda = {3,2,1,0}. Check each is genuinely\n   supported on that weight only, and record which sectors survive in the rep. *)\nwith2 = Select[Keys@sectors[testrep, 2], AllTrue[sectorVec[testrep, testrep, #], PossibleZeroQ] === False &];\nTable[{nu, Min[{testrep[[1]] - nu[[1]], testrep[[2]] - nu[[2]], nu[[3]] - testrep[[3]], nu[[4]] - testrep[[4]]}] + 1,\n   DeleteDuplicates[Pick[allWts, Unitize[sectorVec[testrep, testrep, nu] /. a[__] -> 1], 1]] === {nu}}, {nu, with2}] // TableForm",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
