   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Rectangular reps $[S,S,0,0]$: monomial labels as CG indices\n\nFor $\\lambda=[S,S,0,0]$ the weights $\\lambda-e_1+e_2=\\{S{-}1,S{+}1,0,0\\}$ and $\\lambda-e_3+e_4=\\{S,S,{-}1,1\\}$ do not occur in the irrep (their dominant rearrangements are not $\\le\\lambda$), so\n$$\\langle HWS|E_{12}=\\langle HWS|E_{34}=0$$\non top of the generic $\\langle HWS|E_{21}=\\langle HWS|E_{43}=0$. Thus $\\langle HWS|$ is annihilated by the *entire* Levi $\\mathfrak{gl}(2)\\oplus\\mathfrak{gl}(2)$ off-diagonal part — it is an extreme vector for the parabolic, and the four **commuting** operators $E_{13},E_{14},E_{23},E_{24}$ (the abelian nilradical) generate the whole dual module. Verified below: the monomial covectors have rank $=\\dim$.\n\nThe catch is that they are a **spanning set, not a basis**. In a weight sector with margins $m$, there are $\\min(m)+1$ monomials but the weight multiplicity is only\n$$\\mathrm{mult}(\\mu)=\\min\\big(\\min(m)+1,\\ S+1-\\max(m)\\big),$$\nverified for $S=1..4$. The two agree iff $\\min(m)+\\max(m)\\le S$; otherwise the monomials are linearly dependent. Globally the over-completeness is exactly $\\dim[S{-}1,S{-}1,0,0]$ (excess $1,6,20,50$ against $\\dim=6,20,50,105$). Truncating each sector to its first $\\mathrm{mult}(\\mu)$ values of $t$ recovers an honest basis.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "rect[S_] := {S, S, 0, 0};\n\n(* (a) The extra annihilation conditions, absent for non-rectangular reps.\n   Columns: <HWS|E12, <HWS|E34, <HWS|E21, <HWS|E43 (max abs entry). *)\nbraKill[rep_] := Max@Abs[UnitVector[dim[rep], 1] . EE[rep] @@ #] & /@ {{1, 2}, {3, 4}, {2, 1}, {4, 3}};\nTableForm[{#, braKill[#]} & /@ {rect[1], rect[2], rect[3], {3, 2, 1, 0}, {2, 1, 1, 0}},\n  TableHeadings -> {None, {\"rep\", \"{E12, E34, E21, E43}\"}}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
