  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### How rich are rectangular reps really?\n\nContrast with the symmetric powers $[S,0,0,0]$: there the Levi is $\\mathfrak{gl}(1)\\oplus\\mathfrak{gl}(3)$, the nilradical is the *three* commuting $E_{12},E_{13},E_{14}$, and monomials of degree $\\le S$ are already a basis — the ideal is just \"everything of degree $>S$\", with **no relations at all**. That is the genuinely trivial case: a truncated free polynomial ring, all weight multiplicities $1$.\n\nRectangular reps are strictly richer: weight multiplicities run up to $S+1$, there is a real relation, and there is a nontrivial $D$-filtration. But the extra richness is *exactly one integer's worth* — the power of $D$ — because $\\mathrm{Gr}(2,4)$ is a single quadric (the Klein quadric) in $\\mathbb{P}^5$. Equivalently, via $\\mathfrak{su}(4)\\cong\\mathfrak{so}(6)$:\n$$[S,S,0,0]\\ \\cong\\ \\text{traceless symmetric degree-}S\\text{ tensors on }\\mathbb{C}^6\\ =\\ \\text{spherical harmonics }\\mathcal{H}^S(\\mathbb{C}^6),$$\nconfirmed by the dimension identity $\\tfrac{(S+1)(S+2)^2(S+3)}{12}=\\binom{S+5}{5}-\\binom{S+3}{5}$ (checked $S=1..6$), with $D$ playing the role of the invariant quadratic form $r^2$. So they are \"as rich as spherical harmonics\": not $\\mathfrak{gl}(2)$-like, but the classical, fully-understood harmonic structure — one step up from free, not wild.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (j) Symmetric powers [S,0,0,0] for comparison: 3 commuting generators, monomials of\n   degree <= S are already a basis (no relations), and E23/E24/E34 also kill the bra.\n   Then the so(6) harmonic dimension identity for the rectangular case. *)\nsymVec[rep_, {a_, b_, c_}] := UnitVector[dim[rep], 1] . mpow[EE[rep][1, 2], a] . mpow[EE[rep][1, 3], b] . mpow[EE[rep][1, 4], c];\nsymTest[S_] := Module[{rep = {S, 0, 0, 0}, L},\n   L = Select[Flatten[Table[{a, b, c}, {a, 0, S}, {b, 0, S}, {c, 0, S}], 2], Total[#] <= S &];\n   {S, dim[rep], Binomial[S + 3, 3], Length[L], MatrixRank[symVec[rep, #] & /@ L],\n    Max@Abs@Flatten[UnitVector[dim[rep], 1] . EE[rep] @@ # & /@ {{2, 3}, {2, 4}, {3, 4}}]}];\nColumn[{TableForm[symTest /@ {2, 3, 4}, TableHeadings -> {None, {\"S\", \"dim\", \"C(S+3,3)\", \"#monomials\", \"rank\", \"E23/E24/E34 on bra\"}}],\n  TableForm[Table[{S, (S + 1) (S + 2)^2 (S + 3)/12, Binomial[S + 5, 5] - Binomial[S + 3, 5]}, {S, 1, 6}],\n   TableHeadings -> {None, {\"S\", \"dim[S,S,0,0]\", \"so(6) harmonics\"}}]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
